recomp.patch - what the Godot side needs changed in tools/recomp (rt, render, sound, app, net, net2).
tools/godot/build.py applies it to its snapshot (`snapshot`), and writes it again from the snapshot (`patch`: the text
up to the first "diff -ru" line - these notes - is kept).  From the workspace root:
    patch -p1 -d tools/recomp --dry-run < tools/godot/recomp.patch

ONE HUNK IN IT (2026-10-13 23:35, the Godot side, docs/issues/native-godot.md "FOURTH ROUND"): net2/launch.cpp - the big
lock is let go around the game's own calls in do_choose / do_launch.  Found in a Godot program running a room through
RtaNet2: on_tasks held net2impl::big_lock() while do_launch called the game (fn_0019d028), the game reached a vertical
blank and waited for the host's next step (the library gates every blank, rtag.cpp), and the host - Godot's main thread
- was waiting for the same lock in net2_poll: both programs stood still at "the room started" (sampled stacks).  With the
hunk the same flow runs (see that section).  rta_app / n2_headless never block a blank on their own net2 caller, so
they do not need it, but it is right for them too.  MERGED into tools/recomp/net2/launch.cpp by the coordinator on 2026-10-13; this file holds no hunk again.

Before that hunk NOTHING was in it (2026-10-13 21:40, docs/issues/native-app.md 13.1): its three pieces are merged into
tools/recomp, so a snapshot of the shared tree needs no patch, and build.py does not hand a file without a hunk to patch(1).

What was in it, and where it is now:

1. sound/audio_out.cpp - the sound device is the host (RTA_AUDIO_HOST: tools/godot/lib/audio_host.inc).  Only the
   library is compiled with the macro; nothing changes for rta_app.  In tools/recomp/sound/audio_out.cpp.

2. sound/drivers.cpp - THE MUSIC'S OWN VOLUME (rta_sound_set_music_gain; stream 2 of the stream driver is the music).
   In tools/recomp/sound/drivers.cpp.  The library hands it out as rtag_set_option("music_volume", "0..1"); the
   stand-alone program as --music-volume, the settings line music_volume and "app option music_volume V".

3. THE GAME'S OWN HUD, SECOND GROUP (the boss meter and one-line message, the prompt box): 1d93b0 and 1d99f0 are in
   tools/recomp/hle.txt and both translations were made again; render/layout.h (M_TEXT), render/gs.h and gs.cpp
   (Gs::hide_text), app/gfx_rt.cpp (the two wrappers) are in tools/recomp.  A build whose translation lacks the two
   addresses still defines RTA_NO_HUD_TEXT_HOOKS (tools/godot/build.py does so by itself).  The library's switch is
   rtag_set_option("game_hud_text", "off"); the stand-alone program's --game-hud-text off.
